"""Tracked-version registry — site data for weisssrv-lib's check-versions.py.

`task maintenance:check-versions` reads this file (the checker's default lookup
path) and compares each entry's upstream against the pin in `vars_file`;
`task maintenance:update-version SERVICE=<name>` rewrites the pin and
regenerates the cluster-versions ConfigMap.

What ships here is the PLATFORM set — an entry for EVERY pin in `vars_file`,
including the ones the optional modules add. Add an entry per application you
adopt (its `var_name` is the key in the vars file, so a typo shows up as "pin
not found"), and delete the entry for anything you remove.

Coverage is enforced, not trusted: `task lint:version-coverage` (and the CI job
of the same name) runs `check-versions.py --check-coverage`, which fails when a
pin in `vars_file` has no entry here. Without that gate the weekly
version-bump-bot stays green while silently never reporting the untracked pins —
the failure mode is invisible precisely because the pin does not exist in the
checker's world. A pin with genuinely no upstream to track goes in
`untracked_allowlist` WITH a rationale, never in neither place.

This file is rendered from the template, so its entries follow the same
`{% raw %}{% if %}{% endraw %}` conditions as the pins in
ansible/inventories/prod/group_vars/all.yml — an entry whose pin was never
generated would report "unknown" forever.

Field reference: weisssrv-lib docs/SCRIPTS.md. Categories are
github | dockerhub | ghcr | lsio | helm | apt_repo | manual, each with its own
fetch fields. `held: True` reports an upstream but never writes it — say why in
`notes`, which is the most valuable column in this file.
"""

# Charts reconciled by Flux: nothing to deploy, the push is the deploy.
_FLUX = "git push (Flux reconciles)"


def _chart(name, key, repo, chart, **extra):
    entry = {
        "name": name,
        "var_name": f"helm_chart_versions.{key}",
        "category": "helm",
        "helm_repo": repo,
        "helm_chart": chart,
        "deploy_command": _FLUX,
    }
    entry.update(extra)
    return entry


